        <p class="eyebrow">The mark in the sky</p>
        <h2 id="elephantulus-title">Six circles. Two legs.<br>Eight stars.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="elephantulus-prose">
        <p>The seanslab elephant is built from six circles—the body, head, three-part trunk, and circular eye cutout—and two rounded rectangles for its legs. Keep only the center of each primitive and the silhouette becomes an eight-star asterism.</p>
        <p>Connected in the same order, those points retain the curled trunk, the backward glance, the round body, and its two-footed stance. We call it <em>Elephantulus</em>: the little elephant, held still in starlight.</p>
        <p class="elephantulus-formula"><span>6 circles</span><b>+</b><span>2 legs</span><b>→</b><span>8 centers</span><b>→</b><span>1 asterism</span></p>
      </div>
    </section>

